{"availability":"available","full":"bikramtuladhar/handpress","name":"handpress","description":"Edit a hand-written static site in place, in the browser. Saves are git commits.","category":"Other","language":"JavaScript","stars":2,"forks":0,"created":"2026-09-26T05:32:20Z","updated":"2026-10-04T06:47:11Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://handpress-demo.bikramtuladhar2011.workers.dev","topics":["cloudflare-workers","cms","contenteditable","editable","git-based-cms","git-cms","handpress","headless-cms","html","inline-editing","no-build","static-site","wysiwyg"],"demo":"https://handpress-demo.bikramtuladhar2011.workers.dev/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-05T05:50:51.226Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-05T05:50:51.226Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-05T05:50:51.226Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-04T06:52:21.152Z","stars":2,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-05T05:50:51.226Z","stars":2,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Let a client edit a hand-written static site — the real pages, in place, in the browser. No CMS, no build step, no database. Every save is a git commit.","Most CMSs ask you to break a design into templates and move the words into a database. That is the right trade for a publication with a thousand posts. It is the wrong trade for a brochure site of ten careful pages, where the layout is the product and the owner wants to fix a date or swap a photograph twice a year.","Handpress keeps the HTML as the source of truth and teaches the browser to edit it."],"features":["No templating. Your markup is untouched except for a small data-e key per editable element.","No database. Files in git. Before Save the editor has its own Undo; after it, git revert. Backups are your repository.","No build. One JavaScript file, loaded only for signed-in editors. Visitors download nothing.","Clean diffs. A changed sentence is a one-line diff you can review in a pull request.","The design can't drift. New entries are copies of existing ones, so a client cannot invent a layout."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/bikramtuladhar/handpress/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"dcb55083776c999bddbc7791bd7305bca0937d41e22cdb6ceb08c8711991f765","extractedAt":"2026-10-04T06:52:21.239Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-04T06:52:21.239Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Let a client edit a hand-written static site — the real pages, in place, in the browser. No CMS, no build step, no database. Every save is a git commit.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/bikramtuladhar/handpress/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"Sign-in needs a Google ID token that Google validates, plus a match on the admin list.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/bikramtuladhar/handpress/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"The only outside hosts are accounts.google.com (the sign-in button),","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/bikramtuladhar/handpress/blob/main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"dcb55083776c999bddbc7791bd7305bca0937d41e22cdb6ceb08c8711991f765","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/bikramtuladhar/handpress/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-04T06:52:21.239Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-04T06:47:11Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/bikramtuladhar/handpress/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-04T06:52:21.241Z","hash":"dcb55083776c999bddbc7791bd7305bca0937d41e22cdb6ceb08c8711991f765","originalBytes":11591,"storedBytes":11591,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["page","handpress","browser","site","edit","file","pages","save","any","editor","new","one","admin","every","google","html","npm","only","edits","list","live","npx","test","text","add","client","docs","edited","github","images","key","keys","own","public","skills","undo","what","writes","build","click","data","each","example","files","footer","header","install","it.","javascript","kept",